NS1 or M2-2 protein is highly attenuated and immunogenic in chimpanzees</article-title><source>J Virol</source><year>2000</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>9317</fpage><lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10982380</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/JVI.74.19.9317-9321.2000</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Erbacher</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Zou</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bettinger</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Steffan</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Remy</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chitosan-based vector/DNA complexes for gene delivery: biophysical characteristics and transfection ability</article-title><source>Pharm Res</source><year>1998</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>1332</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9755882</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1023/A:1011981000671</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Illum</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nasal drug delivery&#x02013;possibilities, problems and solutions</article-title><source>J Control Release</source><volume>87</volume><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>98</lpage><comment>2003 Feb 21;</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12618035</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kumar</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Behera</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Lockey</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhullar</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>De La Cruz</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Leong</surname><given-names>KW</given-names></name><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohapatra</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intranasal gene transfer by chitosan-DNA nanospheres protects BALB/c mice against acute respiratory syncytial virus infection</article-title><source>Hum Gene Ther</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>1415</fpage><lpage>25</lpage><comment>2002 Aug 10;</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12215263</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1089/10430340260185058</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kumar</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kong</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Behera</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Hellermann</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name><name><surname>Lockey</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohapatra</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chitosan IFN-gamma-pDNA Nanoparticle (CIN) Therapy for Allergic Asthma</article-title><source>Genet Vaccines Ther</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>3</fpage><comment>2003 Oct 27;</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14613519</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1479-0556-1-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pison</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Welte</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Giersig</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Groneberg</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nanomedicine for respiratory diseases</article-title><source>Eur J Pharmaco